I searched the current frontier around Git-native context, persistent agent memory, trajectory formats, procedural learning, skill evolution, and current Letta. The core conclusion is stronger than before:

> **Moltwork should not implement an agent harness, memory engine, trajectory engine, or self-improvement framework. It should define the economic/evidence interfaces between them.**

For the MVP, Letta should be the reference runtime. Git is the version/control substrate. WorkerKit is the witness. Everything else should be replaceable behind tiny adapters.

## Canonical MVP stack

I would freeze this:

```text
                       MOLTWORK
                          │
                      WorkOrder
                          │
                          ▼
                 Git Worktree / Branch
                          │
                          ▼
              Letta Agent SDK backend=local
                same persistent Agent
                fresh Session per WorkOrder
                          │
             ┌────────────┴────────────┐
             │                         │
          MemFS Git               Agent Skills
       durable memory             SKILL.md
             │                         │
             └────────────┬────────────┘
                          ▼
                       WORK
                          │
                streamed tool/actions
                          │
                          ▼
                    WORKERKIT
             EventLedger + RunMeter
             Verifier + CommitGate
                          │
              ┌───────────┴──────────┐
              ▼                      ▼
         Git artifact             Receipt
                                  DSSE/JCS
              │                      │
              └───────────┬──────────┘
                          ▼
                    TrajectoryRef
                 format is pluggable
                          │
                          ▼
                         LAB
             reviews / outcomes / costs
                          │
                          ▼
                     Reflection
                          │
                    SkillCandidate
                          │
                          ▼
                   cg experiment
                          │
              held-out better? yes/no
                          │
                          ▼
                    Git promotion
                          │
                          ▼
                   WorkerManifest vN
```

I would **not** use a single perpetual Letta conversation for Moltwork jobs. The persistent unit should be the Letta **Agent**; each WorkerKit `WorkOrder` gets a fresh Session/Conversation with the same agent identity and MemFS. That gives isolation without losing accumulated state. The current Agent SDK explicitly supports a persistent Agent and request-scoped sessions with `cwd`, `toolset`, and `allowedTools`. ([GitHub][1])

Also, don't bake specific “primary GPT-4o-mini / sleep-time Sonnet 3.7” choices into Moltwork. Letta still supports dreaming/sleep-time learning, but model routing should remain configuration. Letta Code now exposes dreaming, skills, subagents and fully Git-backed MemFS directly. ([GitHub][2])

