# Tier 1 — directly steal these ideas

## 1. Git Context Controller — GCC

This is extremely aligned.

The central primitives are exactly the right ones:

```text
COMMIT
BRANCH
MERGE
CONTEXT
```

for context rather than inventing yet another retrieval service. The original paper models long-horizon agent context as a persistent versioned hierarchy. Later revisions report over 80% on SWE-Bench Verified and >13% improvement over strong long-context baselines; the original SWE-Bench-Lite result was 48%, so the apparent conflicting numbers come from different paper revisions/benchmarks. ([arXiv][5])

Paper:

[https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.00031](https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.00031?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

Original project:

[https://github.com/theworldofagents/GCC](https://github.com/theworldofagents/GCC?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

There is also a separate lean GCC-v2-inspired implementation that stores hashes/intents and reconstructs detailed context from Git instead of duplicating verbose summaries:

[https://github.com/faugustdev/git-context-controller](https://github.com/faugustdev/git-context-controller?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

### What Moltwork should steal

Not GCC's agent.

Just:

```text
checkpoint
fork
merge
reconstruct
```

You already have real Git.

So WorkerKit needs only a tiny `WorkspaceRef`:

```json
{
  "repo": "...",
  "baseCommit": "...",
  "branch": "mw/run/123",
  "headCommit": "...",
  "worktree": "..."
}
```

The rest is Git.

