# 3. `lhw/opencode-plugin-git-memory`

Your description was accurate. I verified the actual repo.

It stores memory on a detached/orphan `memory/agent` branch using Git blobs, trees and commits, and advances the ref atomically using `git update-ref`. It doesn't dirty the working tree. It also implements compact context loading and time-decay ranking.

[https://github.com/lhw/opencode-plugin-git-memory](https://github.com/lhw/opencode-plugin-git-memory?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

**Do not install its OpenCode memory system into Letta.**

Steal the storage trick.

For Moltwork-generated **Lab memory that is separate from Letta cognition**, detached refs are elegant:

```text
refs/moltwork/runs
refs/moltwork/assets
refs/moltwork/decisions
```

But Letta MemFS itself should remain Letta's Git repository.

