# Trajectory: important correction

You don't actually need to choose one trajectory implementation forever.

Define:

```python
TrajectoryRef(
    format,
    schema,
    uri,
    sha256,
    run_id
)
```

Then any trajectory standard can plug in.

## Letta `trajectory`

For the **MVP I would use this first**.

It already normalizes:

```text
Claude Code
Codex
Copilot CLI
Cursor
Droid
Gemini CLI
Hermes
Letta Code
OpenClaw
OpenCode
OpenHands
Deep Agents
...
```

into one validated model-ready representation. Crucially, Letta Code is already a supported source. ([GitHub][7])

[https://github.com/letta-ai/trajectory](https://github.com/letta-ai/trajectory)

Packages:

```text
@letta-ai/trajectory
agent-trajectory
```

This means your homemade `lab/trajectory.py` should largely disappear.

---

## OpenTrajectory

I would still support this.

It's more explicitly **eval-first**: ordered steps, tool calls, outcomes and evaluator-filled verdicts, with a JSON schema, validator, conformance corpus and OpenTelemetry mapping. Its current adapters include Claude Code, Codex, Antigravity and LangGraph; its reference judge distinguishes harness failures from training/reward problems and product/capability failures. ([GitHub][8])

[https://github.com/abhid1234/opentrajectory](https://github.com/abhid1234/opentrajectory?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

My division would be:

```text
Letta trajectory
    = ingestion/normalization layer

OpenTrajectory
    = optional portable evaluation artifact
```

Don't make WorkerKit depend on either schema.

WorkerKit stores only:

```text
TrajectoryRef
```

That is the nimble design.

