# ReasoningBank

Paper:

[https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.25140](https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.25140?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

Code:

[https://github.com/google-research/reasoning-bank](https://github.com/google-research/reasoning-bank?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

ReasoningBank explicitly learns from **both success and failure**, distilling generalizable reasoning strategies rather than storing raw trajectories. It then uses retrieved reasoning memories to guide subsequent tasks. ([arXiv][11])

For Moltwork this reinforces:

```text
FAILED run != worthless run
```

A rejected hackathon approach can still generate:

```text
decision
failure lesson
test harness
module
negative constraint
```

But ReasoningBank itself does not need to become a dependency.

