# ReMe — dynamic refinement

Paper:

[https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.10696](https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.10696?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

Current open-source implementation:

[https://github.com/agentscope-ai/ReMe](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/ReMe?iZPWMW=lLIVnG22rC8JWa&utm_source=chatgpt.com)

ReMe focuses on avoiding the “append-only memory dump” failure through success/failure/comparative distillation, context-sensitive reuse and **utility-based refinement/pruning**. The project is now a sizable local-first file/Markdown memory system. ([ACL Anthology][12])

### For Moltwork

Steal:

```text
utility
refinement
deprecation
```

Don't install ReMe alongside Letta MemFS for MVP.

That would give you two competing memory authorities.

