# Agentic Context Engineering — ACE

Paper:

[https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.04618](https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.04618?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

ACE treats context as an evolving playbook and uses generation/reflection/curation with **incremental delta updates** rather than constantly rewriting summaries. It specifically targets “context collapse,” where repeated summarization slowly destroys useful details. ([arXiv][17])

There is an independent MIT-licensed reproduction:

[https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/agentic-context-engineering](https://github.com/rrahimi-uci/agentic-context-engineering?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

This gives you another good rule:

> **Learning promotion should patch context incrementally, not regenerate the entire Worker memory.**

That fits Git perfectly.

